          "content": "### Approach: Fixed-size sliding window\n\nTwo strings are anagrams if they have the same character frequencies. Since the string contains only lowercase ASCII letters, we can represent frequencies with an array of size 26.\n\n1. Count frequencies of characters in the pattern.\n2. Count frequencies of the first window in the string, whose length equals the pattern length.\n3. Compare the two frequency arrays. If equal, the window is an anagram.\n4. Slide the window one character at a time:\n   - Add the new character entering the window.\n   - Remove the old character leaving the window.\n   - Compare frequencies again.\n5. Store the starting index whenever the frequencies match.\n\n### JavaScript implementation\n\n```js\nfunction findAnagrams(s, p) {\n  const n = s.length;\n  const m = p.length;\n\n  if (m === 0 || m > n) return [];\n\n  const need = new Array(26).fill(0);\n  const window = new Array(26).fill(0);\n\n  const base = 'a'.charCodeAt(0);\n\n  // Count pattern characters\n  for (let i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n    need[p.charCodeAt(i) - base]++;\n  }\n\n  // Count first window characters\n  for (let i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n    window[s.charCodeAt(i) - base]++;\n  }\n\n  const result = [];\n\n  function isAnagram() {\n    for (let i = 0; i < 26; i++) {\n      if (need[i] !== window[i]) return false;\n    }\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  if (isAnagram()) {\n    result.push(0);\n  }\n\n  // Slide the window\n  for (let i = m; i < n; i++) {\n    window[s.charCodeAt(i) - base]++;          // add new character\n    window[s.charCodeAt(i - m) - base]--;      // remove old character\n\n    if (isAnagram()) {\n      result.push(i - m + 1);\n    }\n  }\n\n  return result;\n}\n\nconsole.log(findAnagrams(\"cbaebabacd\", \"abc\"));\n```\n\n### Output\n\n```js\n[0, 6]\n```\n\n### Explanation using the example\n\nFor:\n\n```js\ns = \"cbaebabacd\"\np = \"abc\"\n```\n\nThe pattern `\"abc\"` has length `3`, so we check every window of length `3`:\n\n- Index `0`: `\"cba\"` → anagram of `\"abc\"` ✅\n- Index `1`: `\"bae\"` → not an anagram\n- Index `2`: `\"aeb\"` → not an anagram\n- Index `3`: `\"eba\"` → not an anagram\n- Index `4`: `\"bab\"` → not an anagram\n- Index `5`: `\"aba\"` → not an anagram\n- Index `6`: `\"bac\"` → anagram of `\"abc\"` ✅\n- Index `7`: `\"acd\"` → not an anagram\n\nSo the starting indices are:\n\n```js\n[0, 6]\n```\n\n### Complexity\n\n- Time: `O(n * 26)`, which is effectively `O(n)` because the alphabet size is fixed.\n- Space: `O(1)`, since the frequency arrays always have size `26`.",
